To show you how **Joined Inheritance** works from end-to-end, we will build the "Gadget Store."

In this setup, you will see how Hibernate handles the "Splitting" logic. Even though you save a single object in Java, Hibernate will perform multiple inserts into different tables.

I have added a `CommandLineRunner` (the "Bootstrapper") which will automatically insert dummy data the moment you hit "Run."

---

### 📂 1. The Entities (The Architecture)

```java
// PARENT CLASS
@Entity
@Inheritance(strategy = InheritanceType.JOINED) // This creates separate tables
@Getter @Setter
public abstract class Gadget {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;
    private String brand;
    private double price;
}

// CHILD 1
@Entity
@Getter @Setter
public class Laptop extends Gadget {
    private int ramSize;
    private String processor;
}

// CHILD 2
@Entity
@Getter @Setter
public class Smartphone extends Gadget {
    private int batteryCapacity;
    private boolean is5G;
}

```

---

### 📂 2. The Repository (The Universal Key)

You only need **one** repository for the parent. Hibernate will automatically know which child table to look into based on the ID.

```java
@Repository
public interface GadgetRepository extends JpaRepository<Gadget, Long> {
    // This single repo can find Laptops, Smartphones, or all Gadgets
}

```

---

### 📂 3. The Service (The Strategy Switch)

The logic here is identical to Single Table. This proves that the **Strategy Pattern** in your Java code is independent of the Database strategy.

```java
@Service
public class GadgetService {

    @Autowired
    private GadgetRepository gadgetRepository;

    public Gadget saveGadget(String type, String brand, double price, int spec1, String spec2, boolean spec3) {
        Gadget gadget;

        if (type.equalsIgnoreCase("LAPTOP")) {
            Laptop laptop = new Laptop();
            laptop.setRamSize(spec1);      // spec1 = RAM
            laptop.setProcessor(spec2);    // spec2 = Processor
            gadget = laptop;
        } else {
            Smartphone phone = new Smartphone();
            phone.setBatteryCapacity(spec1); // spec1 = Battery
            phone.set5G(spec3);              // spec3 = is5G
            gadget = phone;
        }

        gadget.setBrand(brand);
        gadget.setPrice(price);

        return gadgetRepository.save(gadget);
    }
}

```

